# ElderWise — agent rules

Authority when conflicted: `PRD.md` > `Architecture.md` > `Rules.md` > `Phases.md` > agent suggestion. Fix docs; don't work around them in code.

**Source of truth:** `main` on GitHub is the only authoritative copy of the docs and schema. Never treat local caches, chat uploads, email attachments, or stale working copies as authoritative — always read from the repo on `main` (or the branch you are actively merging into `main`).

## Track ownership (Track A only)

- **Build:** Next.js dashboard, onboarding, auth UI, care circle, SOS history/display, reports, settings — anything a human clicks.
- **Do NOT build:** n8n workflows, Meta/WhatsApp send/receive, scheduling, reminders, escalation, STT, SOS dispatch/nudges (WF-4). That is **Track B** (Robert / n8n).
- Systems meet **only at Supabase**. Next.js never sends WhatsApp. n8n never renders UI. n8n never calls Next.js.
- **One exception:** authenticated **server-side** SOS-resolution webhook Next.js → n8n (`Architecture.md`). Not a precedent for a second exception.
- SOS UI cascade / `active|acknowledged|…` = **display only**. Real behaviour = parallel CT + optional LCT + optional Doctor, 4 nudges / 2 min, `sos_events.status` `open|resolved`.

## Non-negotiables (N1–N6)

| # | Rule |
|---|---|
| **N1** | Never diagnose / medical advice / clinical inference — facts only, route to humans. |
| **N2** | SOS path is sacred — no silent failure, no auto-close, never behind routine traffic. |
| **N3** | Never guess for the elder — re-ask if unclear. |
| **N4** | Never add to elder surface area — WhatsApp only; no app/login for the elder. |
| **N5** | Elder consents herself; silence ≠ consent; nothing scheduled until `consent_confirmed_at` is set. |
| **N6** | Data isolation via **RLS on every table** — not app-code hope. |

## Working rules

- Before code: read `PRD.md`, `Architecture.md`, `Rules.md`, `Templates.md` from the repo (prefer `main`). **Docs are the spec; the codebase may be wrong.** Do not cite pinned version numbers across companion docs — file name only.
- Do not invent features, fields, tables, or endpoints. Uncertain → **ask**; never fill gaps with a confident guess.
- Must-haves only unless team lead expands scope (`Rules.md` S1–S3).
- Schema: migration in `/supabase/migrations` with **RLS in the same migration**. No ad-hoc Supabase dashboard edits.
- Secrets: never client-side; never in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`. Service-role key = server/n8n only.
- **No RAG / pgvector / embeddings** — care-circle lookup is relational (`Architecture.md` §3.1).
- Naming: `Architecture.md` §5.5 glossary (Loved One=EP, Care Partner=CT, Local Buddy=LCT, Family Doctor=DR; check-in/SOS status maps).
- Stack is fixed (`Architecture.md` §3). No new deps/services without asking.
- Product spelling: **ElderWise**. English-only MVP copy.
